{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HANDOFF (session paused, ticket left in_progress — do not reopen/reclaim, just resume in this worktree).\n\n**State of the uncommitted work** (worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/compliant-lemon-grunion-impl`, branch `compliant-lemon-grunion-impl`, on top of `d42744e020b3`):\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py` — modified, NOT committed. Contains a worktree-based fix for the repo_root/tickets_root conflation bug: `materialize_reconstructed_ticket()` now does `git worktree add <scratch> HEAD --detach` against the real project (so code-grounded criteria G3/G4/T8 see real source instead of an empty scratch dir), mounts a fresh throwaway ticket tracker on that worktree, and `full_mode_request_criteria()` now computes the per-ticket routed criteria set (not the raw full registry) via `route_criteria`. Cleanup via `git worktree remove --force` (never bare `shutil.rmtree`).\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier2.py` — modified, NOT committed. 44/44 unit tests passing, including one asserting the scratch root literally contains a real committed source file.\n- Lint/typecheck/complexity/module-size all clean per the implementer's last report.\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/ledger.jsonl` — modified (grew with new commissioning rows). Total epic-wide ledger spend as of this pause: **$33.63 / $200 cap**.\n- Two untracked scratch report files exist and are NOT meant to be committed as final evidence: `tier2-current-9d77c4897604.md`, `tier2-current-b704c15897fc.md`.\n\n**OPEN PROBLEM — the fix has NOT resolved the degenerate signature.** Two full 20-sample commissioning runs were executed with this exact worktree-based fix in place (code unchanged since):\n- `tier2-current-9d77c4897604` (finished 2026-08-31T03:38:48Z, $8.06): Mean Jaccard 0.0, newly_blocking=0, relieved=19/20.\n- `tier2-current-b704c15897fc` (finished 2026-08-31T05:36:45Z, $7.02): Mean Jaccard 0.0, newly_blocking=0, relieved=19/20.\n\nBoth are still degenerate — essentially identical to the pre-fix signature. This means the repo_root/code-grounding fix, while a real and verified bug fix (confirmed via unit test and single-ticket qualitative check), was **not sufficient** to explain the aggregate Jaccard≈0/relieved≈19-20-of-20 pattern. A single-ticket sanity check earlier in this investigation showed qualitatively correct behavior on ONE sample, but that did not generalize to the aggregate — a caution against declaring victory on n=1.\n\n**No process is currently running.** No live tier2 process, no `tier2-scratch-*` worktree remains, and the delegate fork from the prior investigation is no longer listed as an active agent (it appears to have exited after its last report).\n\n**Gerrit change 2450** (this ticket's harness change): still at patchset 2 or earlier — NOT re-pushed with this fix. Patchset 1 CI-failed (model-provenance ratchet, since fixed); patchset 2 CI-passed but LLM-Review rejected on a global-vs-per-ticket criteria bug (also fixed in the current uncommitted diff). This session was unable to re-verify current Gerrit vote state (credential helper in this non-interactive shell returned \"Device not configured\" — needs an interactive session or a working credential store). **Do not commit/push until the degeneracy is actually understood or resolved** — the repo_root fix should still land as a real bug fix, but the ticket's own AC (finding-set Jaccard/verdict-flip report) is not yet demonstrating non-degenerate behavior.\n\n**Recommended next investigation angles** (not yet tried):\n1. Check whether `verify_findings`/`pass3_decide` on the CANDIDATE side is actually receiving the candidate's fresh Pass-1 findings, or whether it's silently falling back to an empty/stale finding set (would explain relieved≈19-20/20: everything \"verified away\").\n2. Check whether the STORED baseline being diffed against is itself the right population — i.e. whether `norm_id` matching between candidate and stored findings has a systematic mismatch (e.g. a routing/prompt-id namespace change between when the corpus was frozen and now) that makes every finding look \"new\" to the Jaccard calc regardless of content.\n3. Consider instrumenting one single-sample full-mode run with verbose intermediate output (candidate findings JSON + stored findings JSON side by side) rather than only the aggregate report, to see concretely why they're not intersecting.\n4. Re-examine whether `route_criteria`'s per-ticket filtering (added in this fix) is now excluding criteria that the STORED corpus actually included at review time (a routing-config-drift possibility, distinct from the repo_root bug already fixed).\n\nResuming session: read this comment, `git diff src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py`, and the two untracked `.md` reports before continuing. Do not discard the uncommitted diff — it is a verified, real, but insufficient fix."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788215005337090517,"uuid":"c043ea19-f6ea-4d5c-9f10-1f547a339474"}